From: Shiro836 <17294277+Shiro836@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:00:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/23] waydroid-nvidia: rm-integration

nvidia-prolapse/driver-source/native/mesa/rm-integration.patch at waydroid-nvidia 788728d3d51c (v0.2.0-rc12), sha256 54fca6552808611a43e9de374af8894bda7407966ded470fd114df7ce1412d97, with nvkmd_rm.c (2f926aec5d6f7b48a290cc5564281025f02ba2b8c9e13a67a8907f350f5e9c04), nvkmd_rm.h (ca896494425926d651e2f5a4468ddc4b9aee99f9eecde9548909e8ccaa3ac948) and nv_rm.h (608a6bfe2599ce9b6cad139f2db3506b774a9e3dd0f69f9c8263c89296bddfd6) copied unchanged into src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/rm/.

Merged with ANAL-240 by hand: the graphics family keeps two queues
(nvk: advertise two queues in the graphics queue family), the
sparse-image check goes before ANAL-240's tiling local, the RM
compressed-kind helper sits before nvk_image_init_common() and the
compression policy lives in nvk_image_init_layout(), and libvulkan_nouveau
keeps the common ICD version script next to -lnv_bionic_native.

Clean-room tree: the image compression policy and the comments describing
another driver are removed; see stubs S4 and S5 in SPEC.md.
